      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm doing some planning for a cedar deck build in vancouver. i need to walk through the basics of calculating live load vs dead load for the beam and post sizing. can u explain the difference and how they factor into the total load? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Live load and dead load are the two main types of weight you'll be dealing with for your cedar deck in Vancouver. Dead load is the permanent weight of the structure itself, like the wood, hardware, and decking materials. Live load is the temporary weight, which includes people, furniture, snow, and anything else that might be placed on the deck. You need to calculate both to determine the required strength of your beams and posts, ensuring they can handle the total combined load without collapsing.",
